"""A turn that cannot do its work ends FAILED now, raised as an alarm — never reported "done".

WHY. 2026-10-27, ACE turn 599fad3b on cloud-ec2-2: its first Drive call came back
"Method doesn't allow unregistered callers" (ACE's Drive server still wanted a
key file its vault no longer held). The turn then emailed the person who asked —
an outside counterpart — that "this runner has no logins", marked her thread read,
and finished `done`. Nothing alarmed; the only trace was in her inbox. Jonathan:
"this should be a clear error generated by Canopy that causes the turn to not even
get finished and creates an error and alarm to resolve."

So an abort is one call, made by the canopy plugin's `credential_guard` hook the
moment a tool fails on credentials (or by the agent, `canopy turn abort`):

* the turn ends FAILED with the reason as its note, through `close_turn` — so
  `auto_debug.on_turn_failed` opens (or counts) the failure investigation, raises
  its `turn_failure` alert and starts the debugger's turn, exactly as for any
  other failed turn. Nothing here is a second alarm path;
* an `error` event says so where the conversation is shown;
* a box still running the session is told to stop it (`runner.cancel`), so the
  agent does not go on to tell anyone. Its later finish is an idempotent no-op.

A turn already DONE can still be aborted: a laptop turn is finished the moment its
Claude session exists (`turn_agent_tokens`, "laptop sessions"), so the work — and
the failure — happens after. Any other terminal status is left as it is.

There is deliberately no list of what an agent "should" have: the agent's vault
is the one declaration of its secrets, and the dependency that failed on
2026-10-27 was never in it. The failure itself is the signal.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

from .closing import close_turn
from .ledger import append_events
from .models import Turn
from .routing import EXECUTING

#: The statuses an abort moves to FAILED (see the module docstring for DONE).
ABORTABLE = (*EXECUTING, Turn.DONE)
REASON_MAX = 1500


class NotAbortable(Exception):
    """The turn ended some other way (cancelled, lost, missed); nothing changed."""


def abort_note(reason: str, tool: str = "") -> str:
    reason = " ".join((reason or "").split())[:REASON_MAX] or "no reason given"
    where = f" in {tool}" if tool else ""
    return f"Aborted by canopy: the turn could not do its work{where}. {reason}"


def abort(turn: Turn, *, reason: str, tool: str = "", by: str = "") -> Turn:
    """End `turn` FAILED with an abort note; idempotent on a turn already FAILED."""
    if turn.status == Turn.FAILED:
        return turn
    if turn.status not in ABORTABLE:
        raise NotAbortable(f"status={turn.status}")
    was_executing = turn.status in EXECUTING
    note = abort_note(reason, tool)
    event = {"aborted": True, **({"tool": tool[:200]} if tool else {}), **({"by": by} if by else {})}
    if not close_turn(turn, Turn.FAILED, note, from_states=ABORTABLE, event=event):
        if turn.status == Turn.FAILED:
            return turn
        raise NotAbortable(f"status={turn.status}")
    append_events(turn, [{"kind": "error", "payload": {"detail": note}}])
    if was_executing and turn.claimed_by_id:
        from apps.realtime import groups

        groups.publish(groups.runner_group(turn.claimed_by_id),
                       {"type": "runner.cancel", "turn_id": str(turn.id)})
    return turn
